# The maker: a record without a value stands for each closure that the literal alone takes, and the scope is listed once, for the field that no name finds.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: [[scope]]: env {{*}} = NewObject
# CHECK: [[add]]: f4 @Void = NewClosure [[scope]] function=f4 closureForm=Deferred [isMadeOnDemand]
# CHECK: [[get]]: f5 @Void = NewClosure [[scope]] function=f5 closureForm=Deferred [isMadeOnDemand]
# CHECK: = NewObject -, [[add]], [[get]], {{*}}, [[scope]] layout=L0 fields=[0, 1, 2, 3]
# A call through a slot: the read of the slot has one reader, which takes what the closure captures. The emitter loads the scope out of the object and nothing out of the slot.
# RUN(CALLS): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CALLS-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CALLS: [[closure]]: f4 @Cell = GetDeferredClosureSlot {{*}}key="add" {{*}}# uses=1 onlyUser=[[capture]]
# CALLS-NEXT: [[capture]]: env {{*}} = GetCapture [[closure]] function=f4
# Where the allocation is in sight the call asks the slot all the same: what the allocation lists says nothing of what has been stored since (a-closure-that-lies-in-its-slot-answers-for-its-own-scope-1).
# RUN(INSIGHT): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# INSIGHT-LABEL: code f3:Body
# INSIGHT: [[read]]: {{*}} = GetDeferredClosureSlot
# INSIGHT-NEXT: = GetCapture [[read]]
# RUN(WITHHELD): walk f1 mechanisms=all-Deferral
# WITHHELD-NOT: closureForm=Deferred
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
